    "title": "Parkway East 'Bathtub' Flood Project Starts Next Week, Ramps Closing Into 2027 - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Derrick Wright ,\n1 days ago PennDOT crews will start preparatory work Thursday, October 1, on a $14.34 million project to fix the flood-prone stretch of Parkway East known as the “Bathtub,” with long-term ramp closures and lane restrictions following just two days later. The project targets the low-lying section of I-376 between the Grant Street interchange and the Fort Pitt Bridge in Downtown Pittsburgh, an area that has flooded and shut down traffic repeatedly for decades. Read full article",
